		Annotation {
		  SID			  "3:360"
		  Name			  "This subsystem receives data from force sensors in the KINARM setup, and starts and stops the data trans"
		  "fer in response to changes in\nthe force sensor parameters in the system above. Each KINARM EP can have a force se"
		  "nsor, so there can currently be up to two in a \ngiven setup. The force sensors transmit data over UDP, and parame"
		  "ters of the data transfer (such as the data rate and IP address) are\nconfigured for each force sensor individuall"
		  "y via a web interface they provide. BKIN preconfigures force sensors with IP addresses \n192.168.0.10-11, where th"
		  "e first address is given to the sensor for robot 1 and the second to that for robot 2."
		  Position		  [24, 55]
		  HorizontalAlignment	  "left"
		  ZOrder		  -1
		}
		Annotation {
		  SID			  "3:359"
		  Name			  "Each subsystem also handles the receiving of data from its particular sensor. When a sensor is indicated"
		  " as present, the latest data from \nits IP is unpacked and placed into a 1x6 array (zeros are explicitly specified"
		  " when a sensor is indicated as not present). The arrays for\nthe individual sensors are combined into a 2x6 matrix"
		  ", similar to how robot data is handled in the system above.\n\nEach packet received from a force sensor contains t"
		  "he following:\n     sequence number [uint32]\n     internal sequence number [uint32]\n     system status code [uin"
		  "t32]\n     x-axis force [int32]\n     y-axis force [int32]\n     z-axis force [int32]\n     x-axis torque [int32]\n"
		  "     y-axis torque [int32]\n     z-axis torque [int32]\n\nFor more information, again see the ATI Net Interface gu"
		  "ide."
		  Position		  [24, 345]
		  HorizontalAlignment	  "left"
		  ZOrder		  -2
		}
		Annotation {
		  SID			  "3:358"
		  Name			  "Each \"force sensor x\" subsystem here starts and stops the data transfer from its respective force sens"
		  "or. When the input flag indicating \nthe presence (1: yes, 0: no) of a force sensor changes, the respective subsys"
		  "tem sends a command message via UDP to that force \nsensor's IP address that starts or stops the data transfer acc"
		  "ordingly. For details about the structure of the command message, see the \nATI Net Interface guide. \n\nNote that"
		  " the default setting for all force sensors is 1, for \"present\", in the system above. This is done so that whenev"
		  "er BKIN's client \nsoftware applies hardware settings to a task program, it must first lower all force sensor flag"
		  "s and then raise those for whichever sensors\nare present again. This forces all sensors off in case they were not"
		  " stopped properly by a previous task. This would not stop data that \nhad been transmitted from being received, so"
		  " when a force sensor is marked as not present the data is zeroed explicitly."
		  Position		  [24, 165]
		  HorizontalAlignment	  "left"
		  ZOrder		  -3
		}
	      }
	    }
