    Block {
      BlockType		      SubSystem
      Name		      "GUI Control"
      SID		      "1"
      Ports		      [1, 2]
      Position		      [50, 100, 230, 220]
      ZOrder		      1
      BackgroundColor	      "[0.858820, 0.690190, 0.309800]"
      MinAlgLoopOccurrences   off
      PropExecContextOutsideSubsystem off
      RTWSystemCode	      "Auto"
      FunctionWithSeparateData off
      Opaque		      off
      RequestExecContextInheritance off
      MaskHideContents	      off
      Object {
	$PropName		"MaskObject"
	$ObjectID		24
	$ClassName		"Simulink.Mask"
	Type			"GUI Control"
	Description		"<b>Do not rename this block, it must be called 'GUI Control'.</b>\n<p>\nThis block allows the GUI to co"
	"ntrol the Task Program.  In particular, the order and control of trials is implemented via this block.  \n<p>\nThis b"
	"lock also defines the target preview information to show the user on the GUI, i.e. the display of greyed-out versions"
	" of all visual targets defined in the Task Protocol, as well as the display of the \"logical\" versions of the target"
	"s used for hand-in-target calculations.  In order for the GUI to show this target information for a task, the columns"
	" of the target table that define the positions and visual and logical characteristics of targets need to be specified"
	" here."
	Help			"Used by the GUI to control the Task Program\n\n<H2>Library </H2>\nGeneral\n\n<H2>Description </H2>\n<b>Do not"
	" rename this block, it must be called 'GUI Control'.</b>\n<p>\nThis block allows the GUI to control the Task Program."
	" In particular, the order and control of trials is implemented through the use of this block.  \n<P>\nThis block also"
	" tells the GUI which preview target information to show the user (i.e. greyed-out display of all targets in the Task "
	"Protocol). In order for the GUI to show target information for a task, the correct columns in the target table need t"
	"o be specified in the dialog box (see below).\n<P>\nThere are 2 inputs to this block:\n<P>\n<B>Repeat_Trial_Flag: </B"
	"> this scalar input is examined by the GUI Control block at the end of a trial to determine if the trial that just fi"
	"nished should be repeated. If it is greater than 0 <i>and</i> if the GUI has requested to \"repeat error trials\", th"
	"en the trial just finished will be added to a repeat block that will commence at the end of the present block.  If th"
	"is input equals 0 <i>or</i> if the GUI has requested not to \"repeat error trials\", then the trial will not be queue"
	"d for repetition.\n<P>\n<B>e_End_Trial:</B> this event input is used to indicate that a trial has finished. It should"
	" be an event from a Stateflow chart that is created upon completion of a trial. Upon this event occuring (which occur"
	"s on both rising and falling edge), the outputs of this block will change to reflect the next trial's outputs.\n<P>\n"
	"There are 2 outputs from this block:\n<P>\n<B>Trial_Control: </B> this event output is used to control the stateflow "
	"chart in the Task Program.  There are 2 events muxed together in this output: a 1 kHz clock and an end-trial-now even"
	"t.  The clock is a true 1 kHz clock in that it is 0.5 ms high, 0.5 ms low (i.e. it should trigger an event in the sub"
	"squent flowchart to which it is attached on ONLY the rising edge).  The clock only runs when the GUI has commanded th"
	"e Task Program to run (i.e. when the GUI commands a pause to the Task Program, this clock stops executing).  The end-"
	"trial-now event triggers an event on both the rising and falling edges.   It is triggered by the GUI and pressing of "
	"the Pause button in the GUI when certain conditions apply - these conditions include when the Pause option is: Skip T"
	"rial, Repeat Trial Now or Repeat Trial Later.  Those options in the GUI assume that the end-trial-now event has been "
	"used in the Task Program such that it will cause an immediate exit of the trial.  Please see the Customing Task Progr"
	"ams documentation for more details.\n<P>\n<B>Trial_Protocol</B> this vector output contains the row from the Trial Pr"
	"otocol Table corresponding to the present trial.  It is typically connected to the stateflow chart to implement trial"
	"-specfic behavior.\n<P>\n<B><I>This block must be present in all Task Programs.</I></B>\n\n<H2>Parameters and Dialog "
	"Box</H2>\n<P>The GUI is capable of showing greyed-out versions of all targets in a target table for the user to have "
	"a quick view of all targets in the task protocol.  Similarly, the GUI can also show outlined versions of all the the "
	"'logical' targets (the targets used for hand-in-target calculations) in the task protocol.\n<P>\n<B>Target Type:</B> "
	"the type of preview target to display.\n<P>\n<B>Columns for X and Y Position:</B> the columns in the Target Table use"
	"d to define the x and y positions.\n<P>\n<B>Column(s) for Visual Target Attributes:</B>: the columns that specify the"
	" visual characteristics of a target that are specific to that type of target. These are similar to the target type-sp"
	"ecific columns specified in the Show_Target block.\n<P><I>Circle:</I> radius of the circle (cm).\n<P><I>Ellipse:</I> "
	"major radius (cm), minor radius (cm), rotation angle (degrees).  If no rotation is desired, the rotation column index"
	" should be set to 0.\n<P><I>Rectangle:</I> length (cm), height (cm), rotation angle (degrees).  If no rotation is des"
	"ired, the rotation column index should be set to 0.\n<P><I>Line:</I> end point x-axis position relative to start poin"
	"t (cm), end point y-axis position relative to start point (cm), width (cm).\n<P><I>Triangle:</I> length (cm), height "
	"(cm), offset of peak of triangle relative to midpoint of the length (cm), rotation angle (degrees). If a height colum"
	"n index of 0 is specified, then an equilateral triangle with sides of the specified length is used.  If no rotation i"
	"s desired, the rotation column index should be set to 0.\n<P>\n<B>Column(s) for Logical Target Attributes:</B>: The c"
	"olumns that specify the logical characteristics (used to determine if the hand is in a target or not) of a target tha"
	"t are specific to that type of target. They are of the same format as the visual characteristics for each target, and"
	" can be the same as those columns or different. They are only relevant if using the HandInTarget block. If not using "
	"that block, enter 0 for each logical target attribute column. \n<P>\n"
	Initialization		"% Check the version of MATLAB that is being used, using logic from Mathworks' R12-\n% backwards-comp"
	"atible verLessThan function. More information can be found at:\n%\n% http://www.mathworks.com/support/solutions/data/"
	"1-38LI61.html?solution=1-38LI61\n%\n% If the MATLAB version is R2007b (7.5) or higher, include the s-function used to"
	" \n% disable SMIs on startup. This prevents needless CPU overload errors.\nperformBKINModelSetup();\n\ncurrent_ver = "
	"ver('MATLAB');\ncurrent_ver_parts = sscanf(current_ver.Version, '%d.%d.%d')';\nif length(current_ver_parts) < 3\n    "
	"current_ver_parts(3) = 0;\nend\n\ndesired_ver = '7.5.0';\ndesired_ver_parts = sscanf(desired_ver, '%d.%d.%d')';\nif l"
	"ength(desired_ver_parts) < 3\n    desired_ver_parts(3) = 0;\nend\n\nresult = (sign(current_ver_parts - desired_ver_pa"
	"rts) * [1; 0.1; 0.01]) < 0;\n\ncurrent_block_path = gcb;\npos = get_param([current_block_path '/ICH7'], 'Position');\n"
	"block_type = get_param([current_block_path '/ICH7'], 'BlockType');\n\nidxs = findstr(current_block_path, '/GUI Contro"
	"l');\n[idxCount, n] = size(idxs);\n[m, strlen] = size(current_block_path);\nbColorSet = 0;\nif idxCount == 0 || idxs("
	"1) ~= strlen - 11\n    fprintf('=========ERROR====================\\n');\n    fprintf('%s should be called GUI Contro"
	"l, attempting to rename.\\n', current_block_path);\n    try\n        set_param(current_block_path, 'Name', 'GUI Contr"
	"ol');\n        current_block_path = gcb;\n        fprintf('Rename successful\\n');\n    catch err\n        fprintf('R"
	"ename failed. You may have 2 GUI Control blocks or another improperly named block.\\n');\n       	set_param(current_b"
	"lock_path, 'BackgroundColor', '[0.9, 0, 0]');\n        bColorSet = 1;\n    end\n    fprintf('========================"
	"=====\\n');\nend\n\n\nif result\n    % The MATLAB version is less than 7.5, so the s-function should be removed if pr"
	"esent. \n    if ~strcmp(block_type, 'Constant')\n        delete_block([current_block_path '/ICH7']);\n        add_blo"
	"ck('built-in/Constant', [current_block_path '/ICH7'], 'Name', 'ICH7');\n        set_param([current_block_path '/ICH7'"
	"], 'Position', pos);\n        set_param([current_block_path '/ICH7'], 'Value', '0');\n    end\nelse\n	% The MATLAB ve"
	"rsion is 7.5 or higher, so the s-function should be added if not already there.\n    %if ~strcmp(block_type, 'S-Funct"
	"ion')\n        delete_block([current_block_path '/ICH7']);\n        add_block('built-in/S-Function', [current_block_p"
	"ath '/ICH7'], 'Name', 'ICH7');\n        set_param([current_block_path '/ICH7'], 'Position', pos);\n        set_param("
	"[current_block_path '/ICH7'], 'FunctionName', 'ich10');\n    %end\nend\n\n% Record the xPC Target version in a Consta"
	"nt block for reference by the Dexterit-E GUI.\nv = ver;\n\nfor i=1:length(v)\n    if strcmp(v(i).Name, 'xPC Target')\n"
	"        set_param([current_block_path '/xPC Version'], 'Value', v(i).Version);\n    end\nend\n \n% Record the current"
	" time (i.e. compile time) in a Constant block for reference by the Dexterit-E GUI.\nset_param([current_block_path '/d"
	"lm build time'], 'Value', num2str(now,20));\n\n% Handle the 'Show repeat trial flag input' setting: swap the flag inp"
	"ut with a constant block or\n% vice versa in accordance with the setting (.\nshow_repeat_trial_flag = strcmp(get_para"
	"m(current_block_path, 'show_repeat_trial_flag'), 'on');\nblock_type = get_param([current_block_path '/Repeat_Trial_Fl"
	"ag'], 'BlockType');\n\nif show_repeat_trial_flag && ~strcmp(block_type, 'Inport') || ...  % if a change is required.."
	".\n   ~show_repeat_trial_flag && strcmp(block_type, 'Inport')\n    \n    % ...delete the existing block, ...\n    pos"
	" = get_param([current_block_path '/Repeat_Trial_Flag'], 'Position');\n    delete_line(current_block_path, 'Repeat_Tri"
	"al_Flag/1', 'Task Execution Control Subsystem/1');\n    delete_block([current_block_path '/Repeat_Trial_Flag']);\n   "
	" \n    % ...add an Inport or a 0-value Constant in place of the previous block (according to\n    % the new setting),"
	" update the signal width flag, and then...\n    if show_repeat_trial_flag && ~strcmp(block_type, 'Inport')\n        a"
	"dd_block('built-in/Inport', [current_block_path '/Repeat_Trial_Flag'], 'Name', 'Repeat_Trial_Flag');\n    else\n     "
	"   add_block('built-in/Constant', [current_block_path '/Repeat_Trial_Flag'], 'Name', 'Repeat_Trial_Flag');\n        s"
	"et_param([current_block_path '/Repeat_Trial_Flag'], 'Value', '0');\n    end\n    \n    % ...connect the new block.\n "
	"   set_param([current_block_path '/Repeat_Trial_Flag'], 'Position', pos);\n    add_line(current_block_path, 'Repeat_T"
	"rial_Flag/1', 'Task Execution Control Subsystem/1');\nend\n\n%after correcting the number of columns, redo the column"
	" grabbing\ntarget_type_str=get_param(current_block_path, 'target_type_str');\nXY_text=get_param(current_block_path, '"
	"XYcols');\nV_text=get_param(current_block_path, 'Vcols');\nL_text=get_param(current_block_path, 'Lcols');\n\ncolumnte"
	"xt=strvcat('Target Visualization in GUI', ' ', target_type_str,['X, Y columns: ', XY_text], ['Visual attribute column"
	"(s): ', V_text],['Logical attribute column(s): ', L_text]);\n\n% Create the text label for the block.\ndraw_commands "
	"= 'disp(columntext); ';\n\ninports = find_system(current_block_path, 'LookUnderMasks', 'all', 'FollowLinks', 'on', 'S"
	"earchDepth', 1, 'BlockType', 'Inport');\n\nfor i = 1:length(inports)\n    inport_name = char(get_param(inports(i), 'N"
	"ame'));\n    \n    if strcmp(inport_name, 'Repeat_Trial_Flag')\n        set_param([current_block_path '/Repeat_Trial_"
	"Flag'], 'Port', '1');\n    end\n    \n    draw_commands = [draw_commands 'port_label(''input'', ' int2str(i) ', ''' i"
	"nport_name '''); '];\nend\n\noutports = find_system(current_block_path, 'LookUnderMasks', 'all', 'FollowLinks', 'on',"
	" 'SearchDepth', 1, 'BlockType', 'Outport');\n\nfor i = 1:length(outports)\n    outport_name = char(get_param(outports"
	"(i), 'Name'));\n    draw_commands = [draw_commands 'port_label(''output'', ' int2str(i) ', ''' outport_name '''); '];"
	"\nend\n\nset_param(current_block_path, 'MaskDisplay', draw_commands);\n\nblock_path = gcb;  % store block path, as gc"
	"b may change with block operations\n\n%%% Handle background colours if link status changes.  \ncheckBackgroundColour("
	"block_path, 'General');\n"
	SelfModifiable		"on"
	Display			"disp(columntext); port_label('input', 1, 'e_End_Trial'); port_label('output', 1, 'Trial Control'); port_la"
	"bel('output', 2, 'Trial_Protocol'); "
	Array {
	  Type			  "Simulink.MaskParameter"
	  Dimension		  8
	  Object {
	    $ObjectID		    25
	    Type		    "popup"
	    Array {
	      Type		      "Cell"
	      Dimension		      5
	      Cell		      "Circle"
	      Cell		      "Ellipse"
	      Cell		      "Rectangle"
	      Cell		      "Line"
	      Cell		      "Triangle"
	      PropName		      "TypeOptions"
	    }
	    Name		    "target_type_str"
	    Prompt		    "Target Type"
	    Value		    "Circle"
	    Callback		    "target_type_str=get_param(gcb, 'target_type_str');\nXYcols=[str2num(get_param(gcb, 'XYcols')) 0 0]"
	    ";\nVcols=[str2num(get_param(gcb, 'Vcols')) 0 0 0 0 0 0];\nLcols=[str2num(get_param(gcb, 'Lcols')) 0 0 0 0 0 0];\n"
	    "\nswitch target_type_str(1:3)\n	case 'Cir'\n		numcol=1;\n        set_param(gcb, 'Target_Type', '1');\n	case 'Ell'"
	    "\n		numcol=3;\n        set_param(gcb, 'Target_Type', '2');\n    case 'Rec'\n        numcol=3;\n        set_param("
	    "gcb, 'Target_Type', '3');\n    case 'Lin'\n        numcol=3;\n        set_param(gcb, 'Target_Type', '4');\n    ca"
	    "se 'Tri'\n        numcol=4;\n        set_param(gcb, 'Target_Type', '5');\n    otherwise\n		numcol=1;\n        set"
	    "_param(gcb, 'Target_Type', '1');\nend\n\nset_param(gcb, 'XYcols', mat2str(XYcols(1:2)));\nset_param(gcb, 'Vcols',"
	    " mat2str(Vcols(1:numcol)));\nset_param(gcb, 'Lcols', mat2str(Lcols(1:numcol)));\n\nindices_padding=zeros(2,5);\ns"
	    "et_param(gcb, 'indices_padding', mat2str(indices_padding(:, 1:(5-numcol))));"
	  }
	  Object {
	    $ObjectID		    26
	    Type		    "edit"
	    Name		    "Target_Type"
	    Prompt		    "Target Type (Int)"
	    Value		    "1"
	    Visible		    "off"
	  }
	  Object {
	    $ObjectID		    27
	    Type		    "edit"
	    Name		    "XYcols"
	    Prompt		    "Columns for X and Y Position"
	    Value		    "[0 0]"
	  }
	  Object {
	    $ObjectID		    28
	    Type		    "edit"
	    Name		    "Vcols"
	    Prompt		    "Column(s) for Visual Target Attributes"
	    Value		    "3"
	  }
	  Object {
	    $ObjectID		    29
	    Type		    "edit"
	    Name		    "Lcols"
	    Prompt		    "Column(s) for Logical Target Attributes"
	    Value		    "4"
	  }
	  Object {
	    $ObjectID		    30
	    Type		    "edit"
	    Name		    "indices_padding"
	    Prompt		    "Indices Padding"
	    Value		    "[0 0 0 0;0 0 0 0]"
	    Visible		    "off"
	  }
	  Object {
	    $ObjectID		    31
	    Type		    "edit"
	    Name		    "task_version"
	    Prompt		    "Task version"
	    Value		    "1.0"
	  }
	  Object {
	    $ObjectID		    32
	    Type		    "checkbox"
	    Name		    "show_repeat_trial_flag"
	    Prompt		    "Show repeat trial flag input"
	    Value		    "off"
	  }
	  PropName		  "Parameters"
	}
      }
      System {
	Name			"GUI Control"
	Location		[59, 52, 1522, 1148]
	Open			off
	ModelBrowserVisibility	on
	ModelBrowserWidth	200
	ScreenColor		"white"
	PaperOrientation	"landscape"
	PaperPositionMode	"auto"
	PaperType		"usletter"
	PaperUnits		"inches"
	TiledPaperMargins	[0.500000, 0.500000, 0.500000, 0.500000]
	TiledPageScale		1
	ShowPageBoundaries	off
	ZoomFactor		"100"
