	    Annotation {
	      SID		      "1:148"
	      Name		      "This level of the block controls the execution of the task in accordance with the specified parame"
	      "ters. The Task Clock square wave is used as the underlying clock for the whole task. Outputs from this block ar"
	      "e available to task developers as \noutports or Gotos, and so are documented in the task development documentat"
	      "ion. Inputs are defined as follows:\n\nrun_task_clock_flag: a flag set by BKIN client software; 0 or 1 to suppr"
	      "ess or use the task clock, respectively. If 0, the task control stateflow will not execute, nor will a clock si"
	      "gnal be generated for this block's trial control output or the global_clock \noutput. A setting of 0 will also "
	      "stop other library blocks from sending information out via UDP.\n\ne_end_Trial: an user-input event that causes"
	      " the control machine to, if in a trial, leave that trial and advance to the next.\n\nrepeat_trial_flag: a user-"
	      "input flag that is used when the e_end_Trial event is observed. If 1 at that time, the current TP will be added"
	      " to a list of TPs that will be executed at the end of the block; if 0, no addition will happen. These repeat TP"
	      "s \nare part of the same block, but are treated together as a group once the original block completes. They are"
	      " either randomized all together or not at all according to the original block's definition. Repeat TPs may be a"
	      "dded indefinitely.\n\nuse_repeat_trial_flag: a flag set by BKIN client software; 0 or 1 to override (suppress) "
	      "repeat trials or allow them, respectively. This setting is part of task protocols.\n\nrun_command: a value sent"
	      " by BKIN client software; 0 or 1 to pause or run the task, respectively. This flag is used to run or pause the "
	      "task in response to the input of users. The flag run_task_clock_flag, in contrast, is used to stop and start ex"
	      "ecution of all \nlibrary blocks without stopping and starting the entire model (thus losing its state).\n\npaus"
	      "e_type: an integer value in [0,4] set by BKIN client software to specify what action to take when run_flag is c"
	      "hanged from 1 to 0 during a set. This setting is part of task protocols.\n\nseed: a value set by BKIN client so"
	      "ftware to seed the pseudorandom number generator. This value must be changed from the default whenever a task i"
	      "s loaded or reset to allow the control stateflow to randomize blocks.\n\nuse_task_protocol_block_sequence_flag:"
	      " a flag set by the block mask indicating whether to use the task protocol's block sequence (1) or to use a bloc"
	      "k sequence specified by the task program (0). In the latter case, the block will be given a new \ninput to whic"
	      "h a user can input the block table row defining the block that should be run next. This input will be checked w"
	      "hen a block (including any repeat trials) is finished in response to the end trial event. \n\nnext_task_program"
	      "_specified_block: a value specifying the index of the next block to run if the use_task_protocol_block_sequence"
	      "_flag is not set. When that flag is not set and a block (including any repeated trials) is finished in response"
	      " to the \nend trial event, this input will be used to select the next block to run."
	      Position		      [15, 171]
	      HorizontalAlignment     "left"
	      ZOrder		      -1
	    }
	  }
	}
