	Annotation {
	  SID			  "1:220"
	  Name			  "This block holds the patch version for \nthe TDK thatthe task was built with."
	  Position		  [1324, 109]
	  ZOrder		  -1
	}
	Annotation {
	  SID			  "1:219"
	  Name			  "These are the constants required for eye tracking calculations"
	  Position		  [1049, 515]
	  HorizontalAlignment	  "left"
	  ZOrder		  -2
	}
	Annotation {
	  SID			  "1:218"
	  Name			  "This block records the version of the task, \nwhich can be read by BKIN client software."
	  Position		  [904, 210]
	  HorizontalAlignment	  "left"
	  ZOrder		  -3
	}
	Annotation {
	  SID			  "1:217"
	  Name			  "This block records the BKIN task development library \nversion, which is updated with each new release."
	  Position		  [854, 150]
	  HorizontalAlignment	  "left"
	  ZOrder		  -4
	}
	Annotation {
	  SID			  "1:216"
	  Name			  "Currently the client software makes use of information in the block mask to show\ngreyed-out \"preview\" "
	  "versions of the visual and logical targets present in the task. \nThis behaviour is facilitated by the Preview Targ"
	  "ets Subsystem, which constructs\na specialized vector using the settings from the block mask and the target \ndefin"
	  "itions that is then read by the client software."
	  Position		  [379, 847]
	  HorizontalAlignment	  "left"
	  ZOrder		  -5
	}
	Annotation {
	  SID			  "1:215"
	  Name			  "This block controls set execution and includes all general task parameters that are intended to be modifi"
	  "ed by BKIN client software. These include \ntarget, trial protocol, and block definitions, as well as the block seq"
	  "uence and status variables that control task run/pause behaviour - essentially, all\nparameters controlled by the \""
	  "task protocol\" are contained here.\n\nThis level of the block collects all the parameters that are intended to be "
	  "set via the mask or BKIN client software, as well as all the Goto symbols \nmade available by the block. Any other "
	  "parameters to be read or written outside of this block should be placed at this level. The task execution \ncontrol"
	  " subsystem performs the actual control of task execution using these parameters. \n\nThose parameters used to creat"
	  "e Goto symbols directly are collected at the left, and all other parameters are connected directly to the subsystem"
	  "."
	  Position		  [19, 125]
	  HorizontalAlignment	  "left"
	  ZOrder		  -6
	}
	Annotation {
	  SID			  "1:214"
	  Name			  "The mask records the xPC Target version as a float \nin this constant, which can be read by client softwa"
	  "re \nto check the xPC version used to build the model."
	  Position		  [854, 90]
	  HorizontalAlignment	  "left"
	  ZOrder		  -7
	}
	Annotation {
	  SID			  "1:213"
	  Name			  "For versions of MATLAB 7.5 (R2007b) and higher, \nICH7 is made an S-Function that disables SMIs."
	  Position		  [854, 30]
	  HorizontalAlignment	  "left"
	  ZOrder		  -8
	}
	Annotation {
	  SID			  "1:212"
	  Name			  "Every Goto block must have at least one corresponding \nFrom block or an error will be generated during t"
	  "he build\nprocess. To ensure that no warnings occur due to this block, \nall Gotos defined by this block also have "
	  "a corresponding\nFrom defined. Those From blocks that are not used by the\nblock are collected inside the subsystem"
	  " at the right."
	  Position		  [1039, 842]
	  HorizontalAlignment	  "left"
	  ZOrder		  -9
	}
	Annotation {
	  SID			  "1:211"
	  Name			  "This block records the current \ntime when the task is built."
	  Position		  [959, 265]
	  HorizontalAlignment	  "left"
	  ZOrder		  -10
	}
      }
